# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hotel Reservation System — environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Database (Neon PostgreSQL) ---
# Pooled connection string used by the application at runtime.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST.neon.tech/DBNAME?sslmode=require"
# Direct (non-pooled) connection string used by Prisma CLI for migrations.
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST.neon.tech/DBNAME?sslmode=require"

# --- Authentication (Better Auth) ---
# Generate a secret with: openssl rand -base64 32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="replace-with-a-32+char-random-secret"
# Public URL of this application (used for auth cookies/callbacks, secure
# cookies, and trusted origins). MUST be an https:// URL in production.
BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# --- Production notes ---
# - Public self-registration is disabled. Staff accounts are created only via
#   the admin portal (ADMIN role) or `staffService.create`.
# - Better Auth rate limiting (sign-in etc.) and the app-level rate limiter
#   are enabled; both default to in-memory storage. For multi-instance
#   deployments, swap in a distributed store (see README "Rate limiting").
